{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1208103-paradigm-assistnace-for-a-new-player","id":1208103,"title":"Paradigm Assistnace for a new player?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-17T12:32:39-07:00","id":1208103,"title":"Paradigm Assistnace for a new player?","content":"So I made a post recently asking about character creation, and got some helpful responses that I am appreciative of, but they highlighted an important detail for me. <br /> <br /> Something I've been struggling with a great deal, and was wondering if you all might be able to help with is conceptualizing a paradigm that can do what I want/need of it? <br /> <br /> There is two main things I've noticed about paradigms. One is that most push you towards abilities that seem more useful for justfiying your magic than actually doing things on their own, such as hypertech or science (Yes, these are ocassionally useful, but it requires special or uncommon circumtances compared to, say, awareness or even research), and the other is that the tools and focuses lend themselves to either downtime only casting, or in the moment casting, with limited overlap, and it is difficult, in my mind, to find a way to make a paradigm that can handle both, feasibly.<br /> <br /> So what I was hoping for help with was coming up with a paradigm that could realistically manage long-term downtime casting for potent effects and buffs, and yet not be overly constrained in high octane situations like rooftop parkour or car chases, and secondly that isn't restrained by ability choice. <br /> <br /> By restrained I mean that I would quite like it if the abilities that were best suited to the paradigm were what I like to call &quot;actionable&quot;: Abilities that are proactive and useful for in the moment, which is distinct from abilities like Esoterica and Crafts, which very rarely serve to let you do things in the moment or to help you overcome immediate and unexpected obstacles. Investigation, computer, and kinda lore/occult are the minimally actionable abilities that seem palatable really, as they're useful proactively, consistently, and hard to replicate usefully even with downtime and outside aid. <br /> <br /> I've looked at the Cult of Ecstasy, the Order of Hermes and the Akashic Brotherhood as possibly fitting that style, although the last is couched a bit too heavily in mysticism that I struggle with to be viable I should think. A more magical bent is preferred to a technological one, although being able to use guns and fast cars/bikes is cool.<br /> <br /> Literally any and all ideas are useful, I'm just trying to broaden my outlook and get multiple perspectives. Don't worry about trying to fit a paradigm more specifically to me or my character, you can just list whatever you come up with and it'll almost certainly help. I really do appreciate any amd all input that you can offer, as really I'm looking for a wide variety of perspectives and ideas to draw from for inspiration. Thanks again. <br /> <br /> Side Note: What books from pre-m20 would be best to look at for getting an expanded perspective on the capabilities of the various spheres?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T16:24:44-07:00","id":1208229,"title":"","content":"M20 Paradigms are broad enough that any of them support potent downtime casting, and quick casting in action scenes. It's only as you start mixing in Practices and Instruments that you risk pushing yourself towards one more than the other.<br /> <br /> Remember that the Abilities listed are suggestions, not requirements unless optional rules are in-play and you plan on using specific Abilities as Instruments.<br /> <br /> You don't need to look outside of M20 really. M20 core has lots of spells in it. While controversial, M20 How Do You Do That was the first Mage book ever to actually be all about this. M20 Book of Secrets can help here too.<br /> <br /> If you go to the older books... you're mostly just going to be looking a sample effects throughout lots of different books; which can be hard since they're often biased samples meant to illustrate things like a Tradition's magical style, or be effects meant for dealing with some aspect of the setting like common effects for traveling into the Umbra and dealing with the consequences of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T16:54:23-07:00","id":1208242,"title":"","content":"Personally I think you\u2019re going about this the wrong way. But then I don\u2019t do Mage as an rpg but as a story.<br /> <br /> Feel free to disregard this if it\u2019s not what you want to get out of this system, but I think you\u2019re going about this backwards.<br /> If I was your ST, I would ask you to think about the kind of character you want to play as. Forget about builds, forget about systems, just focus on the human. The kind of job they have, the life they lived, and the aspirations they may have. From this a character can be constructed, and from this construct everything else can follow.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t concern yourself with what is useful and what you may need, but instead on what this person would be drawn towards, how they believe the universe works, and why it works that way. From that seed a paradigm will be forged.<br /> <br /> Ask yourself the following three questions:<br /> <br /> How do they think reality functions?<br /> How do they believe it is changeable?<br /> What is required to bring about that change?<br /> <br /> From here your focus is decided.<br /> <br /> Disregard M20\u2019s build-a-focus style if you can. I find it unnecessarily categorical.<br /> <br /> Ask yourself how this character lives, what influences them, what matters to them? Which tradition would attract them the most? Which tradition would try to pull them in?<br /> <br /> What aspect of the universe captures their attention? What do they do when they realise the world is sleeping?<br /> <br /> <br /> I highly recommend Revised edition as a good introduction to the spheres. It\u2019s much more succinct then M20, and overall a more comprehensive view with examples and explanations abound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T05:28:51-07:00","id":1208403,"title":"","content":"I agree with the responses above, but there's nothing wrong with wanting to play it mechanically as well!<br /> <br /> If you want something that can be potent in an immediate sense and powerful in a downtime sense, here are two options.<br /> <br /> - Warring Fist Akashic<br /> <br /> Focus: violence, yoga, etiquette, weapons, chanting etc.<br /> <br /> So in a high octane situation you can channel magick through punches, jumps, kicks, acrobatics... and in downtime you can perform ceremonies, train your martial abilities and use yoga and slow/soft martial arts.<br /> <br /> - Hyper-Tech Cyborg<br /> <br /> Focus: brain-computer interface, cybernetics/biotech, hypertech, reality hacking etc.<br /> <br /> In a high octane situation you can channel magick through your augmentations. Your reinforced bones become the focus on a Life 3 Forces 3 punch. In downtime you can create a computer program, build some hypertech, alter your cybernetics... great for making Wonders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}